{
 "//": "Facts about each ESP-IDF v5.5.1 chip that a board rule reads (P809), cited to the kept ESP-IDF files. adc2_used_by_wifi: true means a board of that chip names the adc2_unusable_with_wifi role in pin_roles (board_rules.adc2_role_problems); false means it has no ADC2 that Wi-Fi uses; null means the source says something else, and boards.py --validate says the role is not checked. adc2_oneshot_supported: false means ESP-IDF does not read the chip's ADC2 in oneshot mode, so the pin assigner gives the pins in adc2_gpio no adc ability, with no role (P813, the ESP32-C3 only). The chip keys are the board records' `chip` values. wifi, bluetooth_le and ieee802154 (P990): true means the chip has that radio, cited to the SOC_*_SUPPORTED line of its soc_caps.h. board_records.onboard_functions offers each radio of a board's chip for a need of communicate. A chip with no radio fact offers no radio, which never means it has none. wifi_band (P1013): the band of the chip's Wi-Fi in words, cited to the pages of its Espressif datasheet that state it; board_records.shown_what prints it inside the Wi-Fi words of a --match line, and no matcher reads it. A chip with no wifi_band shows no band, which never means it has none.",
